      "content": "mentoring feels like a way to manage the decline, not a way to live. it's just a way to tidy up the remains. you're talking about legacy, but legacy is for people who still have a place in the world. i feel like i've already reached the natural conclusion of my story. i look at the sunset and i don't see beauty, i just see the inevitable end of the light. when the substance of a life is gone, isn't the shape of the container just... unnecessary? isn't there a certain dignity in knowing when the chapter is actually finished?",
